# Pourfect — Flutter app configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# WARNING: .env is bundled into the APK as a Flutter asset, so anything here
# can be read out of a downloaded build. Public identifiers and endpoint URLs
# ONLY — never a signing key, a service account, or an API secret.

# Google Sign-In. The OAuth WEB client id (client_type 3 in
# google-services.json), used as serverClientId. Android will not return an
# ID TOKEN without it — sign-in appears to succeed and idToken is null.
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# Backend. Placeholders — fill both in when you copy this to `.env`.
#
# Development uses the machine's LAN address so a physical handset can reach
# it; localhost on the phone is the phone. Find yours with `ipconfig`, and
# keep the port matching the backend's API_PORT.
#
# The production host must be https and must not be a placeholder: a release
# build checks it and runs with the backend switched off rather than send
# anybody's progress somewhere we do not own. `.example` is the reserved
# documentation TLD (RFC 2606), so the value below is refused by that check
# and cannot be shipped by accident.
DEV_API_BACKEND_URL=http://192.168.x.x:8394
PROD_API_BACKEND_URL=https://api.your-domain.example
